================================================================================
NO WARRANTY, AND A LIMIT ON WHAT THIS TOOL IS FOR
================================================================================

Provided as-is, without warranty of any kind. Built to teach relationships and
orders of magnitude: what a bridge, a wall, a building or a blockage does to a
river's water level and speed, and roughly where the bed moves or builds up.

It is a teaching model, NOT a flood risk assessment, and it is NOT validated
against measured river levels. It solves one steady flow in one dimension: it
has no time in it, so a short flood would not reach the levels shown; it cannot
follow water round the end of a wall or across a floodplain; buildings report a
depth but do not block the flow; and how deep a bed scours is not modelled. Its
accuracy figures show the engine is consistent with open-channel theory, not
that it matches real rivers. Read docs/method-notes.html, which states every
assumption the code makes and declares what it leaves out.

Do not use it for planning, insurance or construction decisions. For a flood
risk assessment, a planning submission or any figure someone will rely on, use
a validated model, such as HEC-RAS, Flood Modeller or InfoWorks ICM, run by
someone qualified to run it.


