--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
OpenStreetMap — map tiles, place search and river lines, only when asked for
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

River Flow Lab redistributes no OpenStreetMap data. It asks OpenStreetMap's
services only while the Map view is open or a search is made:

  - map tiles from tile.openstreetmap.org, within the OpenStreetMap Foundation's
    tile usage policy;
  - place search from Nominatim (nominatim.openstreetmap.org), within its usage
    policy, at most one search a second;
  - rivers and streams from the Overpass API (overpass-api.de, or
    overpass.private.coffee if the first fails), or from this site's own proxy,
    server/overpass-proxy.php, where it is installed.

That data is © OpenStreetMap contributors and licensed under the Open Database
License (ODbL), https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright. The app credits it on
screen and in every export that holds it, and a reach built from an
OpenStreetMap river says so in its name. A tile service you set yourself in Advanced is used under that
service's terms, with the credit line you give it.


--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Terrain models and other files you load
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

River Flow Lab redistributes no terrain data. A GeoTIFF, ASC or OBJ terrain
model, a 3D model or a project file is read in the browser; nothing is
uploaded anywhere. A terrain model keeps its own licence: Environment Agency
LIDAR, for example, is released under the Open Government Licence v3.0 and
asks for the credit "© Environment Agency copyright and/or database right",
which then travels with images made from it.


--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Test fixtures and fonts
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The test suite answers the map and search requests from tests/fixtures/: a
plain 256 × 256 image made for the tests, not an OpenStreetMap tile, and an
Overpass answer that is synthetic, not OpenStreetMap data.

No web fonts are loaded. The interface uses a system font stack, so no font
licence applies to a deployment of this app.


